Two backend fixes in the existing codebase. Context: everything works correctly when run locally on Streamlit and the final document comes out complete there — but on the frontend/UI (where the code is invoked as a single API call), the report comes back with the tables rendered while the narrative sections and title are empty. Because it works locally on Streamlit, the suspected cause is a Streamlit rerun behavior — i.e. the narrative may only be getting produced on a second pass, effectively as if "Generate Report" has to be hit twice for the narrative to fill in, and the frontend has only a single Generate Report action so that second pass never happens. Fix 1 — Collapse report generation into a single flow: currently the full report is not produced in one execution — the pipeline builds the tables/structured sections first and returns, while the narrative generation (Objective, Background, Conclusion, and the title) only runs on a subsequent pass/second trigger; locally this is masked because the second pass happens naturally, but when the code is invoked as a single API call from the frontend it executes only once, so the tables render while the narrative-dependent sections come back empty, since the step that produces them is never reached in that one execution. The fix is to restructure the flow so that a single call runs every phase sequentially and returns the completed document: parse inputs, build the tables, then call the narrative-generation step unconditionally within the same execution, passing the already-built tables directly as an argument rather than relying on any previously stored/cached state from an earlier pass, and finally assemble and return the finished doc — with no dependence on a second run, second button press, or second iteration to fill the narrative. Fix 2 — Remove the product-name fallback across ALL document types (EI, RS, DEG/EG, BE NOC, and any others): product name must be sourced only from the product_name parameter, so delete every Excel/annexure-derived product-name fallback in every document path with no per-document special casing, and if product_name is missing, fail or flag explicitly instead of silently deriving it from the Excel. Net effect: one single execution that produces tables plus full narrative together, and one single source of truth for product name with no fallbacks anywhere.
